# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# The test of python-constraint-failure.test on a GPU: the flag of the loop
# that tests the group of SHAKE fails the part (D[constraint-failure-stop]).
# With the waters rigid, a restraint of 1e300 on an atom that no constraint
# holds sends it beyond the cell: the build records its stop, the waters
# pass their test, and the part fails with the message of D107 (the
# maintainer's ruling on PR #381).
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_position_guard.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide GPU constraints | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: constraints Double: fails after step 0 and keeps its state; another simulation runs: the constraints of the set 'shake1' failed at step 1: a constrained length is off its target or is not a number
# CHECK: restraint rigid Double: fails after step {{[0-9]+}} and keeps its state; another simulation runs: {{.*}}far outside the cell
# CHECK: constraints Mixed: fails after step 0 and keeps its state; another simulation runs: the constraints of the set 'shake1' failed at step 1
# CHECK: restraint rigid Mixed: fails after step {{[0-9]+}} and keeps its state; another simulation runs: {{.*}}far outside the cell
# CHECK: position guard constraints passed
